{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Behold</b> — because of the desire implanted in a person's heart, it is as though I was fashioned in iniquity. The meaning: for at the time of birth the evil inclination is implanted in the heart." "And the word יחמתני is strange, as though יחמה from me, on the pattern of ליחמנה. And some say: that this alludes to Eve, who did not give birth except after she sinned."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:33.281056997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}